  "n94_definition_excerpts": {
    "zh": [
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#2",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/2/text",
        "text": "爱因斯坦采用了不同的出发点：不为每个否定结果另添一种假说，而把所有惯性参考系遵循相同物理定律作为理论的基础。\n这包括力学过程和电磁过程。\n这里的平等针对物理定律，不是说不同观察者记录的运动轨迹都相同。\n\n静止和匀速直线运动都是相对于所选参考系而言的，没有哪一个惯性系因此在定律上更优越；\n加速运动不属于这个结论。\n迈克尔孙实验未测到当时静止以太模型所预言的地球轨道运动效应，在实验灵敏度范围内支持这一出发点，却不是对所有可能现象的普遍证明。",
        "text_sha256": "d9e279adabb583f44b9dd281fbe7f324bf9b3468e2b92c203fe93d26ff66f557"
      },
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#3",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/3/text",
        "text": "相对性原理是爱因斯坦理论的一个主要公设：**所有惯性参考系中的物理定律具有相同形式**。\n自然过程都遵循这些共同的定律，但各参考系测得的位置、速度和轨迹可以不同。",
        "text_sha256": "9a61028f8f6ca9898b34385917c694ee6875a44d187dc2181c148c704698795b"
      },
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#4",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/4/text",
        "text": "相对性原理要求所有惯性系中的物理定律具有相同形式。\n这是把经典力学的相对性原理推广到包括电磁过程在内的全部物理过程。\n这种推广是理论采用的公设，不是仅凭经典力学就能逻辑证明的结论。",
        "text_sha256": "a99e079ef16af911c98948e91712a55811eb9b85b3ab4e10e77c0d69422b7d01"
      },
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#5",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/5/text",
        "text": "狭义相对论不仅以相对性原理为基础，还有第二个公设：**所有惯性参考系测得的真空光速相同，不随光源或接收机相对该参考系的运动而改变**①。\n它说的是真空中的光速，不是任何介质中的光速，也不是向加速参考系的简单推广。",
        "text_sha256": "5491562b09d3808caee40b496d32910d16c2eec7707f9488c2b7aa7e9d8fd813"
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#2",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/2/text",
        "text": "Einstein chose a different starting point: instead of adding a separate hypothesis for each negative result, he based his theory on all inertial frames obeying the same physical laws.\nThis applies to mechanical and electromagnetic processes.\n\nEquality here concerns physical laws, not identical trajectories recorded by different observers.\nRest and uniform motion in a straight line are relative to the chosen frame, so neither gives an inertial frame a privileged place in the laws.\n\nThis does not erase the distinction between inertial and accelerated motion.\nMichelson's experiment did not detect the effect of Earth's orbital motion predicted by the stationary-ether model being tested.\nWithin the experiment's sensitivity, this supports the starting point rather than proving it for every possible phenomenon.",
        "text_sha256": "0c77fcdd89cf9869bcbf52ed44587f0141d9e3fda9c25bc6cc415589845dfcf0"
      },
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#3",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/3/text",
        "text": "The principle of relativity is a central postulate of Einstein's theory: **physical laws have the same form in every inertial reference frame.**\nNatural processes obey these common laws, although the positions, velocities, and trajectories measured in different frames can differ.",
        "text_sha256": "2f25dc5813b2a24b25f83a9f6b3b6f8a23bf50b21b1e93ced8f13af7b6396d81"
      },
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#4",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/4/text",
        "text": "The principle of relativity requires physical laws to have the same form in all inertial frames.\nIt extends the relativity principle of classical mechanics to all physical processes, including electromagnetic ones.\nThis extension is adopted as a postulate of the theory, not proved by logic from classical mechanics alone.",
        "text_sha256": "e9f2eb6187b4ca8e5bd3bfabdde960b45a1db2d9a4de76b0b82d343fa3469a60"
      },
      {
        "source_ref": "p0252#5",
        "json_pointer": "/prose/5/text",
        "text": "Special relativity also has a second postulate: **all inertial frames measure the same speed of light in vacuum, independent of the motion of the source or receiver relative to that frame.** ①\nThis concerns light in vacuum, not its speed in every material, and is not a simple extension to accelerated frames.",
        "text_sha256": "8afdc50a6b2054b92021e1eb96edbb12aff1c8f6422a09a1db6aebbde741fdfd"
      }
    ]
  },
